+    <section class="journal" aria-labelledby="journal-heading">
+      <p class="eyebrow">From origin to your morning</p>
+      <h2 id="journal-heading">Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <p class="journal-intro">Good coffee begins long before we light the roaster. Here is how we choose the beans behind your daily cup.</p>
+
+      <div id="journal-copy" class="journal-copy">
+        <p>Our sourcing process starts with people and place. Before choosing a coffee, we want to understand who grew it, the landscape it comes from, and the work that went into the harvest. We look for producers and sourcing partners who can trace a lot back to its farm or cooperative and explain how it was picked, processed, and stored. That context helps us make thoughtful decisions and gives us a story we can share with you beyond a country name on a bag.</p>
+        <p>Next comes the tasting table. We roast small samples and cup them side by side, looking for sweetness, balance, and a clear expression of origin. A bright, fruit-forward coffee might become a seasonal filter offering, while a lot with chocolate notes and a rounded body might be a natural fit for espresso. We return to samples more than once, because a memorable first sip matters less than a coffee that keeps tasting good as it cools.</p>
+        <p>Flavor is only part of the decision. We ask our partners about farming practices, water use during processing, and how producers are paid. We value open conversations about costs and the challenges of each growing season, and we aim to build relationships that can continue across harvests. Weather, crop yields, and shipping conditions all change; staying in touch helps us plan responsibly and appreciate the work behind every lot rather than treating coffee as an interchangeable ingredient.</p>
+        <p>When the green beans arrive, we check their condition and compare fresh samples with our original tasting notes. Then we develop a roast profile in small batches, adjusting time and heat to bring out the qualities that made us choose that coffee in the first place. We taste throughout the roast cycle and keep notes so we can refine each batch. From that first conversation at origin to the final brew in our café, our goal stays the same: a delicious cup with a thoughtful, traceable journey behind it.</p>
+      </div>
+
+      <button id="summarize-journal" class="btn" type="button" aria-controls="journal-summary" aria-describedby="journal-status">Summarize</button>
+      <p id="journal-status" class="journal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Get a few key points using your browser's built-in AI. First use may require a model download.</p>
+      <div id="journal-summary" class="journal-summary" aria-labelledby="summary-heading" hidden>
+        <h3 id="summary-heading">The sourcing story, in brief</h3>
+        <ul id="journal-summary-points"></ul>
+      </div>
+      <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to summarize the journal. The full story is available above.</p></noscript>
+    </section>
